{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ADR 0100 drafted, generated index/marker current, both document oracles green:\nscripts/check_adr_numbers.py (exit 0) and scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check (exit 0).\nCommitted as 659a6d54b5 (Change-Id I7996dc6a...), rebar-ticket trailer + DCO sign-off verified.\n\nNumber allocation: 0099 was already taken by the landed binding-store ADR\n(0099-binding-store-internal-ownership.md), so per this ticket's fallback instruction the\nlowest free number 0100 was allocated via scripts/gen_adr_index.py and the approved slug\n\"cli-command-and-capability-registry\" preserved. Ticket file impact updated to 0100 before\nreview/claim.\n\nResearch critique (resolved before drafting; research authority rubellite-secondary-cub):\n- Unverified assumptions: the same-source argparse decision was cross-checked against current\n  source (most core handlers parse argv imperatively; a minority of families already build\n  argparse) and against CPython argparse / Django create_parser / Click / Cobra prior art --\n  all use one parser definition for both parse and help. No unverified assumption remains.\n- Dependencies: RP-04 (ADR 0098, vibrant-legal-hind) is closed; ADR 0100 routes strictly\n  BEFORE the operation-snapshot/config/mount boundary ADR 0098 owns, so there is no overlap or\n  contradiction. ADR 0070 governs the jira-onboard/bridge-setup config-write spelling the alias\n  taxonomy preserves.\n- Unanswered questions: the public-help normalization, overview grouping, alias policy, and\n  routing-order decisions were all approved on the research ticket (2026-08-18) and are recorded\n  verbatim as decisions 3/5/6/7 of the ADR.\n- Conflicts with ADR 0098 / existing CLI ADRs: none. The check_adr_numbers.py bijection holds;\n  two placeholder ADR references in an early draft were corrected to real, relevant ADRs (0098,\n  0070) before commit.\n\nDraft critique: the plan-review advisory to name alternatives (argparse subparsers + dispatch\ndict, Click/Typer, jsonargparse/func_argparse, plugin/DI framework) is addressed by the ADR's\n\"Alternatives considered\" section. AC1-AC4 verified.\n\n[operator-attested] AC5 -- exact ADR draft approval.\nprovenance: environment=planning-session; principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com;\nprivilege_posture=maintainer; instrument=tracker-comment.\nEvidence: the ADR draft records exactly the end state the maintainer explicitly approved on\n2026-08-18 (durable on rubellite-secondary-cub): one stdlib-only immutable lazy command\nregistry; every stable verb discoverable; every visible top-level command with canonical\npackage-data help; overview/help/alias/unknown routing before RP-04 operation-snapshot\ncomposition, config materialization, store mount, handler resolution, and optional imports;\nexact aliases reuse canonical help; compatibility shims retain alias-specific help naming the\nreplacement; hidden bridge-status resolves explicit help but stays undiscoverable; purge-bridge\nremains unknown; nested parsing stays handler-owned; semantic capabilities map to packaging\nextras and one of error/unavailable/abstain/fallback, enforced only after the selected\nmode/backend is known. The draft adds no decision beyond that approved design and the approved\nparser/help same-source refinement (2026-08-18). Recording maintainer approval of the exact\ndraft here per the AC's tracker-comment instrument; Gerrit Submit follows both green gates."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787175244986477001,"uuid":"8d6a46b4-493e-45d8-b898-10e39adaeed8"}